---
source: crates/dreamd-cli/tests/cli_help.rs
expression: "nested_subcommand_help(\"service\", \"install\")"
---
Write a user-scope service for `dreamd watch` (Linux systemd --user unit, macOS LaunchAgent, Windows logon task).

Linux and macOS also start it now. The Windows task first runs at the next logon or on `dreamd service start`, and install also writes the bearer token `dreamd watch` checks, ~/.agent/auth.json.

Usage: install [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --force
          Overwrite an existing LaunchAgent plist (macOS) or scheduled task (Windows); on Windows this also rotates the bearer token. No effect on Linux

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
